msgid "Use JBoss Logging for application logging"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When using the JBoss Logging API, your application requires no additional "
"dependencies, as {project-name} provides it automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid "Get an application logger"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To get an application logger in {project-name}, select one of the following "
"approaches."
msgstr ""

msgid "<<declaring-a-logger-field>>"
msgstr ""

msgid "<<simplified-logging>>"
msgstr ""

msgid "<<injection-of-a-configured-logger>>"
msgstr ""

msgid "Declaring a logger field"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With this classic approach, you use a specific API to obtain a logger "
"instance, store it in a static field of a class, and call logging operations "
"upon this instance."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The same flow can be applied with any of the <<logging-apis,supported "
"logging APIs>>."
msgstr ""

msgid "Define the logger field."
msgstr ""

msgid "Invoke the desired logging methods on the `log` object."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When you create a `Logger` instance, Quarkus keeps metadata associated with "
"the `Logger` name in memory for the full lifecycle of the application."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Do not use an unbounded dynamic name for loggers, for example, `for (int i .."
".) { Logger.getLogger(\"logger-name.\" + i).info(\"my log\") }`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Simplified logging"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus simplifies logging by automatically adding logger fields to classes "
"that use `io.quarkus.logging.Log`.\n"
"This eliminates the need for repetitive boilerplate code and enhances the "
"convenience of logging setup."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The io.quarkus.logging.Log class provides the same methods as JBoss Logging, "
"but as static methods."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The class does not declare a logger field.\n"
"During the application build, Quarkus creates a `private static final org."
"jboss.logging.Logger` field in each class that uses the `Log` API.\n"
"Quarkus uses the fully qualified name of the calling class as the logger "
"name.\n"
"In this example, the logger name is `com.example.MyService`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"During the application build, Quarkus rewrites calls to `Log` methods into "
"JBoss Logging calls on the generated logger field."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use the `Log` API only in application classes, not in external dependencies.\n"
"`Log` method calls not processed by Quarkus at build time will result in an "
"exception."
msgstr ""

msgid "Using <code>io.quarkus.logging.Log</code> in extensions:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"While the `Log` API simplifies logging in application classes, do not use it "
"in extension modules or external dependencies."
msgstr ""

msgid "The following considerations apply:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`io.quarkus.logging.Log` depends on Quarkus bytecode transformations that "
"occur at build time."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In extension modules, `Log` works only if the module includes a Jandex index."
"\n"
"However, this behavior is unsupported and can lead to unreliable logging."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For extension development, use `org.jboss.logging.Logger.getLogger(String)` "
"instead of `io.quarkus.logging.Log`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Injecting a configured logger"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Instead of declaring a logger field, you can use an alternative approach and "
"inject a configured `org.jboss.logging.Logger` instance by using `@Inject`.\n"
"This approach applies only to CDI beans."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To control the logger name, choose one of the following injection patterns:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use `@Inject Logger log` when you want Quarkus to name the logger after the "
"class it is injected into."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use `@LoggerName(\"...\") Logger log` when you want to set the logger name "
"explicitly."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`@Inject` is not required if you already annotated your `Logger` with "
"`@LoggerName(\"...\")`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Once injected, you can use the `log` object to invoke logging methods."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The logger is created with `org.jboss.logging.Logger.getLogger(SimpleBean."
"class)`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In this case, the name \"foo\" is used as a logger name.\n"
"The logger is created with `org.jboss.logging.Logger.getLogger(\"foo\")`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus caches logger instances internally.\n"
"When you inject a logger into a `@RequestScoped` bean, Quarkus shares that "
"logger across bean instances to avoid performance penalties from repeated "
"logger instantiation."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use log levels"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"{project-name} provides multiple log levels to control the amount of "
"information logged based on event severity."
msgstr ""

msgid "Available log levels:"
msgstr ""

msgid "OFF"
msgstr ""

msgid "A special level used in configuration to turn off logging."
msgstr ""

msgid "FATAL"
msgstr ""

msgid "A critical service failure or total inability to handle any requests."
msgstr ""

msgid "ERROR"
msgstr ""

msgid "A major issue in processing or an inability to complete a request."
msgstr ""

msgid "WARN"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A non-critical service error or problem that might not require immediate "
"correction."
msgstr ""

msgid "INFO"
msgstr ""

msgid "Service lifecycle events or other important infrequent information."
msgstr ""

msgid "DEBUG"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Additional information about lifecycle events or events not tied to specific "
"requests, useful for debugging."
msgstr ""

msgid "TRACE"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Detailed per-request debugging information, potentially at a very high "
"frequency."
msgstr ""

msgid "ALL"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A special level to turn on logging for all messages, including custom levels."
""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can also configure the following levels for applications and libraries "
"that use link:https://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/api/java/util/logging/"
"Level.html[`java.util.logging`]:"
msgstr ""

msgid "SEVERE"
msgstr ""

msgid "Same as **ERROR**."
msgstr ""

msgid "WARNING"
msgstr ""

msgid "Same as **WARN**."
msgstr ""

msgid "CONFIG"
msgstr ""

msgid "Service configuration information."
msgstr ""

msgid "FINE"
msgstr ""

msgid "Same as **DEBUG**."
msgstr ""

msgid "FINER"
msgstr ""

msgid "Same as **TRACE**."
msgstr ""

msgid "FINEST"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Increased debug output compared to `TRACE`, which might have a higher "
"frequency."
msgstr ""

