msgid "Configure the log level, category, and format"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"JBoss Logging, integrated into {project-name}, provides a unified "
"configuration for all <<logging-apis,supported logging APIs>> through a "
"single configuration file that sets up all available extensions."
msgstr ""

msgid "To adjust runtime logging, modify the `application.properties` file."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Assuming the link:https://quarkus.io/guides/config-yaml[Quarkus YAML "
"extension] is included, the equivalent YAML configuration is:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When you set the log level to below `DEBUG`, for example `TRACE`, you must "
"also adjust the minimum log level."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Set the minimum log level globally with the `quarkus.log.min-level` "
"configuration property, or set it per category:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The minimum log level is a build-time configuration option that sets the "
"floor level for which Quarkus generates supporting code.\n"
"This enables further build-time optimizations, such as dead code elimination "
"when building a native image."
msgstr ""

msgid "An example from a native executable:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Setting `INFO` as the minimum log level forces checks for lower levels, such "
"as `isTraceEnabled()`, always to return `false`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In turn, code such as `if (logger.isDebugEnabled()) callMethod();` is "
"identified as never executed, also known as dead code."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you add these properties on the command line, ensure the `\"` character "
"is escaped with a backslash:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"All potential properties are listed in the "
"<<loggingConfigurationReference,logging configuration reference>> section."
msgstr ""

msgid "Logging categories"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Logging is configured per category.\n"
"Configuration for a category applies recursively to all subcategories unless "
"a more specific subcategory configuration exists."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The parent of all logging categories is called the \"root category.\"\n"
"As the ultimate parent, this category might contain a configuration that "
"applies globally to all other categories.\n"
"This includes the globally configured handlers and formatters."
msgstr ""

msgid "An example of a global configuration that applies to all categories:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In this example, the root category is configured to use two named handlers: "
"`con` and `mylog`."
msgstr ""

msgid "An example of a per-category configuration:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This example shows how to configure the minimal log level for the categories "
"`org.apache.kafka.clients` and `org.apache.kafka.common.utils`."
msgstr ""

msgid "For more information, see <<loggingConfigurationReference>>."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you want to configure something extra for a specific category, create a "
"named handler like `quarkus.log.handler.[console|file|syslog].<your-handler-"
"name>.*` and set it up for that category by using `quarkus.log.category.<my-"
"category>.handlers`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An example use case can be a desire to use a different timestamp format for "
"log messages that are saved to a file than the format used for other "
"handlers."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For further demonstration, see the outputs of the <<category-named-handlers-"
"example,Attaching named handlers to a category>> example."
msgstr ""

msgid "Property Name"
msgstr ""

msgid "Default"
msgstr ""

msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus.log.category.\"<category-name>\".level"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"INFO footnote:[Some extensions might define customized default log levels "
"for certain categories to reduce log noise by default.\n"
"Setting the log level in configuration will override any extension-defined "
"log levels.]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The level to use to configure the category named `<category-name>`.\n"
"The quotes are necessary."
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus.log.category.\"<category-name>\".min-level"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The minimum logging level to use to configure the category named `<category-"
"name>`.\n"
"The quotes are necessary."
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus.log.category.\"<category-name>\".use-parent-handlers"
msgstr ""

msgid "true"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Specify whether this logger should send its output to its parent logger."
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus.log.category.\"<category-name>\".handlers=[<handler>]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"empty footnote:[By default, the configured category gets the same handlers "
"attached as the one on the root logger.]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The names of the handlers that you want to attach to a specific category."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `.` symbol separates the specific parts in the configuration property.\n"
"The quotes in the property name are used as a required escape to keep "
"category specifications, such as `quarkus.log.category.\"io.quarkus.smallrye."
"jwt\".level=TRACE`, intact."
msgstr ""

msgid "Root logger configuration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The root logger category is handled separately, and is configured by using "
"the following properties:"
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus.log.level"
msgstr ""

msgid "The default log level for every log category."
msgstr ""

msgid "quarkus.log.min-level"
msgstr ""

msgid "The default minimum log level for every log category."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The parent category is examined if no level configuration exists for a given "
"logger category."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The root logger configuration is used if no specific configurations are "
"provided for the category and any of its parent categories."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Although the root logger's handlers are usually configured directly via "
"`quarkus.log.console`, `quarkus.log.file` and `quarkus.log.syslog`, it can "
"nonetheless have additional named handlers attached to it using the `quarkus."
"log.handlers` property."
msgstr ""

msgid "Logging format"
msgstr ""

msgid "Human-readable text"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"{project-name} uses a pattern-based logging formatter that generates human-"
"readable text logs by default, but you can also configure the format for "
"each log handler by using a dedicated property."
msgstr ""

msgid "For the console handler, the property is `quarkus.log.console.format`."
msgstr ""

msgid "The logging format string supports the following symbols:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Symbol"
msgstr ""

msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

msgid "%%"
msgstr ""

msgid "`%`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders a simple `%` character."
msgstr ""

msgid "%c"
msgstr ""

msgid "Category"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders the category name."
msgstr ""

msgid "%C"
msgstr ""

msgid "Source class"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Renders the source class name.footnote:calc[Format sequences which examine "
"caller information might affect performance]"
msgstr ""

msgid "%d{xxx}"
msgstr ""

msgid "Date"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Renders a date with the given date format string, which uses the syntax "
"defined by `java.text.SimpleDateFormat`."
msgstr ""

msgid "%e"
msgstr ""

msgid "Exception"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders the thrown exception, if any."
msgstr ""

msgid "%F"
msgstr ""

msgid "Source file"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders the source file name.footnote:calc[]"
msgstr ""

msgid "%h"
msgstr ""

msgid "Host name"
msgstr ""

msgid "Renders the system simple host name."
msgstr ""

msgid "%H"
msgstr ""

msgid "Qualified host name"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Renders the system's fully qualified host name, which might be the same as "
"the simple host name, depending on operating system configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid "%i"
msgstr ""

msgid "Process ID"
msgstr ""

msgid "Render the current process PID."
msgstr ""

msgid "%l"
msgstr ""

msgid "Source location"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Renders the source location information, which includes source file name, "
"line number, class name, and method name.footnote:calc[]"
