msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Renders all the values from Mapped Diagnostic Context in format `{property."
"key=property.value}`."
msgstr ""

msgid "%x"
msgstr ""

msgid "Nested Diagnostics context values"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Renders all the values from Nested Diagnostics Context in format `{value1."
"value2}`."
msgstr ""

msgid "JSON logging format"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Add the `quarkus-logging-json` extension to enable the JSON logging format "
"and its related configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Add this extension to your build file as the following snippet illustrates:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, this extension overrides the console output format "
"configuration, and any format string or color settings are ignored.\n"
"Other console configuration items continue to apply, including items that "
"control asynchronous logging and the log level."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you prefer human-readable, unstructured logging in dev mode and JSON-"
"structured logging in production mode, configure this by using profiles, as "
"shown in the following configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid "Disable JSON logging in application.properties for dev and test mode:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Choose the JSON console log format by setting the configuration property:"
msgstr ""

msgid "This property sets the JSON log format for the console."
msgstr ""

msgid "The possible values are:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*default*: Generates structured logs based on the key-value pairs present in "
"the log record.\n"
"Mapped Diagnostic Context (MDC) and Nested Diagnostic Context (NDC) data are "
"included under the `mdc` and `ndc` fields."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Set `quarkus.log.console.json.mdc.flat-fields=true` to write MDC entries as "
"root-level JSON fields instead of nesting them under `mdc`.\n"
"This is useful when a log aggregator (such as OpenSearch or Elasticsearch) "
"needs MDC fields to be queryable as top-level document fields."
msgstr ""

msgid "The option is available for all handler types:"
msgstr ""

msgid "console: `quarkus.log.console.json.mdc.flat-fields`"
msgstr ""

msgid "file: `quarkus.log.file.json.mdc.flat-fields`"
msgstr ""

msgid "syslog: `quarkus.log.syslog.json.mdc.flat-fields`"
msgstr ""

msgid "socket: `quarkus.log.socket.json.mdc.flat-fields`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Named handlers, such as `quarkus.log.handler.console.<name>.json.mdc.flat-"
"fields`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*ecs*: Uses the link:https://www.elastic.co/docs/reference/ecs/ecs-field-"
"reference[Elastic Common Schema (ECS)] format.\n"
"This format modifies some default field names and adds other fields to align "
"with ECS."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Fields include `@timestamp`, `log.logger`, `log.level`, `process.pid`, "
"`process.name`, `process.thread.name`, `process.thread.id`, `host.hostname`, "
"`event.sequence`, `error.message`, `error.stack_trace`, `ecs.version`, "
"`data_stream.type`, `service.name`, `service.version`, and `service."
"environment`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"MDC data is kept in the `mdc` field, which is not part of the ECS schema. "
"Set `mdc.flat-fields` to write those entries as root-level fields instead, "
"or add `mdc` to `excluded-keys` to leave them out entirely."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*gcp*: Uses the link:https://cloud.google.com/logging/docs/structured-"
"logging#structured_logging_special_fields[Google Cloud] format.\n"
"This format follows the *default* format."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When you use xref:opentelemetry-tracing.adoc[OpenTelemetry], Quarkus "
"flattens tracing data present in the `mdc` field and copies it to `spanId`, "
"`traceSampled`, and `trace`, with the `trace` value including a prefix."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Google Cloud requires the `trace` field to follow the `\"projects/<my-trace-"
"project>/traces/12345\"` format.\n"
"`<my-trace-project>` uses the value of the `quarkus.application.name` "
"configuration property."
msgstr ""

msgid "Custom JSON fields with JsonProvider"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `JsonProvider` SPI allows you to dynamically inject additional JSON "
"fields into every log record at formatting time.\n"
"Each registered provider's `writeTo` method is called once per log record, "
"receiving a `JsonLogGenerator` and the `ExtLogRecord` being formatted."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Providers can inspect the log record (level, logger name, MDC values, "
"message, etc.) to decide which fields, if any, to add.\n"
"Any keys listed in `quarkus.log.*.json.excluded-keys` are still filtered, "
"even when written by a provider."
msgstr ""

