msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Configure the JSON logging extension using supported properties to customize "
"its behavior."
msgstr ""

msgid "Log handlers"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A log handler is a logging component that emits log events to a recipient.\n"
"{project-name} includes several different log handlers: **console**, "
"**file**, and **syslog**."
msgstr ""

msgid "The featured examples use `com.example` as a logging category."
msgstr ""

msgid "Console log handler"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The console log handler is enabled by default, and it directs all log events "
"to the application's console, usually the system's `stdout`."
msgstr ""

msgid "A global configuration example:"
msgstr ""

msgid "A per-category configuration example:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For details about its configuration, see the xref:#quarkus-"
"core_section_quarkus-log-console[console logging configuration] reference."
msgstr ""

msgid "File log handler"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To log events to a file on the application's host, use the Quarkus file log "
"handler.\n"
"The file log handler is disabled by default, so you must enable it first."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Quarkus file log handler supports log file rotation."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Log file rotation ensures efficient log management by preserving a specified "
"number of backup files while keeping the primary log file up to date and "
"manageable in size."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For details about its configuration, see the xref:#quarkus-"
"core_section_quarkus-log-file[file logging configuration] reference."
msgstr ""

msgid "Syslog log handler"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The syslog handler in Quarkus follows the link:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Syslog[Syslog] protocol, which is used to send log messages on UNIX-like "
"systems.\n"
"It uses the protocol defined in link:https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc5424[RFC "
"5424]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, the syslog handler is disabled.\n"
"When enabled, it sends all log events to a syslog server, typically the "
"local syslog server for the application."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For details about its configuration, see the xref:#quarkus-"
"core_section_quarkus-log-syslog[Syslog logging configuration] reference."
msgstr ""

msgid "Socket log handler"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This handler sends logs to a socket.\n"
"The socket log handler is disabled by default; enable it in your "
"configuration.\n"
"When enabled, it sends all log events to a socket, such as a Logstash server."
""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Typically, this handler is used with the `quarkus-logging-json` extension to "
"send logs in ECS format to an Elasticsearch instance.\n"
"For an example configuration, see the xref:centralized-log-management."
"adoc[Centralized log management] guide."
msgstr ""

msgid "Add a logging filter to your log handler"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can attach a link:https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/17/docs/api/"
"java.logging/java/util/logging/Filter.html[filter] to a log handler such as "
"the console handler.\n"
"The filter determines whether the handler logs a given log record."
msgstr ""

msgid "To register a logging filter:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Annotate a `final` class that implements `java.util.logging.Filter` with "
"`@io.quarkus.logging.LoggingFilter`, and set the `name` property:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In this example, the filter excludes log records containing specific text "
"from console logs.\n"
"The specific text to filter on is not hard-coded; instead, it is read from "
"the `my-filter.part` configuration property."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Attach the filter to the corresponding handler using the `filter` "
